.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKV-DELETE-TABLE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekv-delete-table \- delete a table and everything in it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekv delete-table
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I TABLE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a table and every item in it, and says how many items went with
it.
.PP
There is no undo, no recycle bin and no confirmation prompt. What the
table held is gone when this returns. Export it first with
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-scan (1)
if it is worth keeping.
.PP
The items are removed before the table's own record, so an interrupted
delete leaves items without a table rather than a table nobody can
read. Deleting it again clears them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fITABLE\fR
Table name. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The table is gone; the number of items deleted is printed.
.TP
.B 1
No table of that name exists in this account.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli ekv scan --table deliveries > deliveries-backup.json
euclid-cli ekv delete-table --name deliveries
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekv (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-create-table (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-scan (1)
